import ImpPlusTypes.Typing

/-!
# The hand module of IMP++'s type soundness

HAND-WRITTEN, and empty: the checker `k/impplus-typing.k` accepts programs without variables, so
no cell is typed by hand, and no rule that reads or writes such a cell is reached. Everything is
generated by `k2lean soundness` (`k2lean/docs/design.md`, §3.3) from IMP++'s `imp.k` and the
checker: `Typing.lean` before this module, preservation in `Typed.lean` after it, and `soundness`
in `Soundness.lean`, from IMP++'s `gen --progress` under the typing (`Progress.lean`).
-/
